    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Presenting a fantastic opportunity to acquire a semi-detached property located on the highly desirable Shantalla Road. Boasting approximately 109 square meters of versatile living space, this home offers a wonderful blend of traditional character and excellent potential for modern family living. The property features an attractive red-brick and pebbledash facade, a gated driveway providing secure off-street parking, and a neat front lawn.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, you are greeted by a generously sized hallway highlighted by tall ceilings and decorative coving, offering a welcoming sense of space. Positioned at the front of the house, the expansive living room continues the airy feel with its high ceilings and elegant coving, complemented by a large picture window drawing in abundant natural light and a feature fireplace serving as a focal point. A separate, well-proportioned dining room sits at the rear, offering lovely views out to the back garden. Adjacent to the dining room, the kitchen layout includes a highly practical walk-in pantry under the stairs, providing excellent storage solutions.\r\n\r\nThe upper level is thoughtfully laid out, offering three well-sized bedrooms and a split family bathroom arrangement. The primary bedroom is a superb double room with ample space for large freestanding wardrobes and bedroom furniture. A second large double room is flooded with light and overlooks the rear garden, while the third bedroom, currently utilized as a home office, comfortably accommodates a bed or remains a perfect quiet workspace. The practical split bathroom layout features a separate W.C. and a distinct shower room with a modern sliding glass enclosure.\r\n\r\nA secure side gate leads from the front driveway to the substantial, west-facing rear garden. Primarily laid to lawn and bordered by high, solid block walls and mature shrubs, this private outdoor space captures wonderful afternoon and evening sunlight and offers a blank canvas for those looking to create their ideal garden. The generous plot size also provides tremendous potential for a rear extension, subject to planning permission. \r\n\r\nBeyond the property itself, the home is superbly positioned to enjoy a wealth of local amenities. Beaumont Hospital, Dublin City University (DCU), and the Omni Shopping Centre are all within easy reach, as are the recreational facilities of nearby Ellenfield Park. With excellent public transport links to Dublin City Centre and immediate access to the M1, M50, and Dublin Airport, this home perfectly combines suburban tranquility with exceptional connectivity."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall (2.30m x 4.93m): A generously sized, welcoming foyer with tall ceilings, decorative coving, and access to the main living areas.\r\n\r\nLiving Room (4.02m x 4.30m): A spacious, airy front reception room featuring high ceilings, a large picture window, and a feature fireplace.\r\n\r\nDining Room (3.78m x 3.70m): A well-proportioned rear reception room offering lovely, bright views out to the west-facing garden.\r\n\r\nKitchen (2.54m x 4.16m): Positioned at the rear of the home with convenient immediate access to the adjoining walk-in pantry.\r\n\r\nPantry (0.85m x 1.60m): A highly practical and valuable storage space located cleverly beneath the staircase.\r\n\r\nPrimary Bedroom (3.69m x 4.49m): A superb double bedroom located at the front of the property with ample space for large freestanding furniture.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (3.68m x 3.80m): A bright and spacious second double bedroom flooded with light and overlooking the rear garden.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (2.64m x 3.44m): A versatile front-facing room currently utilized as a home office, but comfortably accommodating a bed.\r\n\r\nBathroom (1.48m x 2.67m): A modern, distinct shower room featuring a sleek sliding glass enclosure and wet-wall finish.\r\n\r\nW.C. (0.75m x 1.49m): A practical separate water closet located immediately adjacent to the main shower room."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Chain Free: Ready for immediate purchase with no onward property chain\r\nPeriod Details: High ceilings and decorative coving in the entrance hall and main living room\r\nOutdoor Space: Substantial, west-facing rear garden capturing afternoon and evening sun\r\nDevelopment Potential: Excellent scope for a rear extension (subject to planning permission)\r\nExcellent Location\r\nSemi-Detached"
      },
